12:["$","article",null,{"className":"relative overflow-hidden rounded-4xl border border-ink/10 bg-paper p-6 shadow-soft sm:p-10","children":[["$","div",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"pointer-events-none absolute -right-20 -top-24 size-64 rounded-full bg-lime/15 blur-3xl"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"relative flex items-center gap-3 border-b border-ink/10 pb-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex size-11 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-teal/10 text-teal","children":["$","$Lf",null,{"icon":{"name":"heart-pulse","size":24,"node":[["path",{"d":"M2 9.5a5.5 5.5 0 0 1 9.591-3.676.56.56 0 0 0 .818 0A5.49 5.49 0 0 1 22 9.5c0 2.29-1.5 4-3 5.5l-5.492 5.313a2 2 0 0 1-3 .019L5 15c-1.5-1.5-3-3.2-3-5.5","key":"mvr1a0"}],["path",{"d":"M3.22 13H9.5l.5-1 2 4.5 2-7 1.5 3.5h5.27","key":"auskq0"}]]},"className":"size-5","aria-hidden":"true"}]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-teal","children":"Treatment overview"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-sm text-ink-soft","children":"Wyoming Family Dentistry · Wyoming, OH"}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"relative mt-2 max-w-none","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"mt-4 text-pretty text-[15.5px] leading-7 text-ink-soft sm:text-base sm:leading-8","children":"The temporomandibular joint (TMJ) is what connects your jaw to your skull, and the key to moving your mouth fluidly. If you have TMJ disorder, it can impact your ability to yawn, eat, and speak, which can be far more than just an inconvenience. TMJ therapy is the treatment that dentists in Wyoming, OH use to not just manage the pain but to improve and abate your condition."}],["$","h3","1",{"className":"text-balance font-display tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mt-9 text-2xl sm:text-[1.65rem]","children":"How Do Dentists Treat TMJ?"}],["$","p","2",{"className":"mt-4 text-pretty text-[15.5px] leading-7 text-ink-soft sm:text-base sm:leading-8","children":"Dentists can treat TMJ via a number of methodologies:"}],["$","ul","3",{"className":"my-5 space-y-2.5","children":[["$","li","0-Relaxation exercises: If",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-[15.5px] leading-7 text-ink-soft","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-[0.7rem] size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-teal"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Relaxation exercises: If your TMJ in Wyoming, OH is caused by jaw tension, a dentist can demonstrate exercises that can help you holistically treat the issue."}]]}],["$","li","1-Appliances: Dental appli",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-[15.5px] leading-7 text-ink-soft","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-[0.7rem] size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-teal"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Appliances: Dental appliances can keep your upper and lower teeth apart, potentially bringing your joints back into alignment for better range of motion."}]]}],["$","li","2-Orthodontics: Taking the",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-[15.5px] leading-7 text-ink-soft","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-[0.7rem] size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-teal"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Orthodontics: Taking the appliance category one step further, a dentist might refer their patients to an orthodontist if they have more severe misalignment and require braces or clear aligners."}]]}],["$","li","3-Surgery: At the most ext",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-[15.5px] leading-7 text-ink-soft","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"mt-[0.7rem] size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-teal"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Surgery: At the most extreme end, you may need surgery to coordinate both the upper and lower jaw. Again, in this case, a dentist may need to refer you to a reputable oral surgeon in the Wyoming area."}]]}]]}],"$L21","$L22","$L23","$L24"]}]]}]
