22:["$","p","5",{"className":"mt-4 text-pretty text-[15.5px] leading-7 text-ink-soft sm:text-base sm:leading-8","children":"Pain management may not correct the issue, but it can be valuable to patients while they’re working on mitigating the disorder. A dentist may recommend anything from hot/cold therapy to medication to help you keep pain at bay."}]
23:["$","p","6",{"className":"mt-4 text-pretty text-[15.5px] leading-7 text-ink-soft sm:text-base sm:leading-8","children":"The best dentists will scale their efforts based on patient symptoms, X-rays, and preferences. As you can tell by the sheer range of treatments, the severity of TMJ disorder can run the gamut. For example, a slight tear in the cartilage of the joint might be resolved in a couple of days while a severely damaged joint could take months to heal."}]
24:["$","p","7",{"className":"mt-4 text-pretty text-[15.5px] leading-7 text-ink-soft sm:text-base sm:leading-8","children":"TMJ disorder may start off barely noticeable and then progress until you can’t ignore it any more. Ideally, you’ll get treatment sooner than later, especially when the disk of your joint might be suffering from continuous erosion. At Wyoming Family Dentistry, we offer therapeutic measures that can do more than just relieve the pain for a night or two."}]
